<Base title="About" description="Why Super Dad’s Cookbook exists and how the recipes are written.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About this cookbook</h1>
      <p>The recipes that get made again and again in our house, written down so they’re easy to find.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Super Dad’s Cookbook started as a stack of notes on the fridge. These are the meals that work on a busy
        weeknight, the breakfasts that can be made ahead, and the treats the kids ask for by name.
      </p>

      <h2>How the recipes are written</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Everyday measurements: cups, tablespoons and teaspoons, not grams.</li>
        <li>Steps in the order you do them, with a time or a visual cue for when each one is done.</li>
        <li>Ingredients you can find at a regular grocery store.</li>
        <li>Tips at the end for swaps, make-ahead plans and leftovers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cooking from your phone</h2>
      <p>
        On any recipe, tap an ingredient to cross it off. Use “Keep screen on while cooking” so your phone doesn’t go
        dark halfway through a step, or print the recipe for the fridge.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
